<title>INDIA: India's Dena Bank issue listed below par at BSE.</title>
<headline>India's Dena Bank issue listed below par at BSE.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of state-run Dena Bank were trading at 28 rupees on the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) after being listed on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The bank had raised 1.8 billion rupees last November through an initial public offer at 30 rupees a share.</p>
<p>Shares of Dena Bank were traded at 28.00 rupees in volumes of over 115,000 shares. The stock saw an early high of 39.75 on Monday but fell back to 28 rupees.</p>
<p>Dena Bank is the country's first state-run bank to be listed in the capital markets in 1997. Bank of India , also state-run, is due to tap the market in the last week of February.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
